ut  it they're very useful for general  functional training because you're  training at different angles having to  cope and deal with the momentum this  makes them the perfect fit for the same  kind of training where you're building  funk  explosive nightwing style strength at  the same time you can use something like  this this is a big kettlebell at waist  36 kilograms you can use that for a  whole bunch of additional things for  instance you can use it to do weighted  pistol squats actually think that  kettlebells are one of the best way to  Train if you're struggling to do leg  work at home because whilst getting a  barbell could be expensive with enough  weight and also take up hollow space a  kettlebell is relatively small and easy  to move around relatively affordable but  you can still do all the things like  squats goblet squats straight legged  deadlift deadlift clean and press all  that stuff and all just this with this  one item that will fit neatly into the  corner of a room that said I do also  have a barbell and my last item here a  battle rake which I attached to this  ladder that has been randomly living  here for an awfully long time battle  ropes are fantastic for resistance  cardio will burn more calories more  quickly by combining something that  taxes the muscle as well as the  cardiovascular system and at the same  time you'll be toning up your shoulders  and yeah battle ropes are fantastic  these are a bit light but again very  cheap and you'll be able to fit it into  a garden or taking me to a park lap  around a tree those are possibilities  the barbell on the other hand I just  used for curls I can also use the  kettlebell here curls it's also useful  for tons more leg exercises and compound  movements I do have a bit more weight in  the shed but this is a good amount to  leave it on I like to just have  everything ready to go something doesn't  grab it I've been using it for lots of  those old time strongman lifts that I've  talked about 